# /opt/xbrain_v6/deploy/env/robot.env -- the LIVE file, not a template.
#
# Per-robot identity: the L5 environment layer (11 S1.1.9.7 whitelist). These are
# the ONLY env keys the config loader (xbrain/common/config/layers.py) accepts;
# anything else set in a runtime process's environment makes config-freeze abort.
#
# WHERE THIS FILE LIVES, AND WHY IT MOVED (user ruling 2026-09-30)
#   It used to be a TEMPLATE at deploy/etc-xbrain/robot.env that a deploy step
#   copied to /etc/xbrain/robot.env and then edited in place. The ruling was
#   "not under /etc, put it under xbrain_v6/deploy". So the copy step is gone:
#   the units read THIS path directly and there is one file, not a template plus
#   an edited copy. Deployment is now self-contained and needs no sudo to create
#   a system directory.
#     Consequence to know about: this file is tracked in git, so editing it for a
#   particular host shows up in git status. That is the intended trade -- the
#   previous shape had the same value in two places with no check that they
#   agreed, which is the failure mode CLAUDE.md 3.6 (iron rule 2) describes for
#   generated config.
#     NOT moved by the same ruling, deliberately: /etc/xbrain/hw_profile (GATE-6,
#   contract 11 S1.1.9.7 says 0444 root:root), /etc/xbrain/branch (the nft branch
#   marker SEC-02 reads) and /etc/xbrain/secrets/ (MED-S5 says verbatim that
#   passwords do NOT go into git). Each carries an ownership or a not-in-git
#   clause that moving it into the repo tree would quietly break, so each needs
#   its own ruling. See 99 DEC-15.
#
# WHO READS THIS
#   - rtk_driver  (ros2_ws/sensor/src/main.cc): XBRAIN_ROBOT_ID is REQUIRED with no
#     default -- the process exits at startup if it is unset. That is deliberate
#     fail-stop: a driver with no rid would publish rt/gnss/* under the wrong key.
#   - p1_motion   (xbrain/p1_motion/runtime/main_wiring.py): the gnss->state/pose
#     bridge is SKIPPED (logs "p1 gnss bridge OFF: XBRAIN_ROBOT_ID unset") when the
#     var is absent, so state/pose goes silent.
#   - config-freeze reads common.robot_id / common.site_id from the RESOLVED snapshot,
#     NOT from this file at runtime. This file is the source the L5 layer reads when
#     the snapshot is built.
#
# THE FAIL-STOP IS UNCHANGED BY THE MOVE
#   Both units reference this path as EnvironmentFile=-<path> (leading -), so the
#   unit still starts when the file is absent and rtk_driver then refuses to start
#   on the missing rid. Setting the rid below does not soften that: delete the file,
#   or comment the line out again, and rtk_driver fail-stops exactly as before. The
#   rid having a value is not the same thing as the guard being gone.
#     Why no placeholder was ever shipped here: a bogus rid (e.g. CHANGE-ME) would
#   let rtk_driver + p1 start and publish under an id the cloud does not know --
#   fail-silent, and 11 FLT-02 makes every message carry it, so the whole uplink
#   would land in a namespace nobody subscribes to.
#
# systemd EnvironmentFile syntax: KEY=value, one per line, no `export`, no surrounding
# quotes.

# --- REQUIRED: this robot's id ---
#
# The VALUE is assigned by the customer cloud, not by us and not by the chassis
# vendor. Ruled by the user 2026-09-30: "gj-001" -- see
# docs/MISSON/新建+Qt->后端心跳+key.md, whose heartbeat sample carries
# "rid": "gj-001", and 11 S2.1 whose grammar is [a-z0-9_-]{1,32}.
#
# *** The example used to read m20s-001, which is the CHASSIS model, not the
# robot's cloud identity. Anyone copying that would have published under an id
# the cloud does not know, and 11 FLT-02 makes every message carry it -- so the
# whole uplink would land in a namespace nobody subscribes to, silently.
#
# "Assigned by the cloud" does NOT mean "delivered at runtime": 11 S15811 puts
# the calibration file at configs/calib/{robot_id}.yaml, so the id must be known
# BEFORE startup, and rtk_driver fail-stops without it (see WHO READS THIS).
# The cloud assigns the value; this file carries it; L5 feeds it into
# common.robot_id when the freeze snapshot is built.
XBRAIN_ROBOT_ID=gj-001

# --- OPTIONAL: site id (maps to common.site_id; used for site-local config) ---
# Left unset: the site is not assigned yet, and site_id's only definition point
# is sites/{site_id}.yaml with the filename AS the value (CFG-CF-7). Inventing
# one here would create a second, contradicting definition.
# XBRAIN_SITE_ID=fire-station-a

# --- OPTIONAL: log level (DEBUG|INFO|WARNING|ERROR); unset -> process default ---
# XBRAIN_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
